---
title: "supabase_client_creation (stem-system: Clubhouse Manager)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_determine_type: caller requests Supabase client
    q_determine_type --> q_create_ssr: createClient() - cookie-based SSR client
    q_determine_type --> q_create_admin: createAdminClient() - service role client
    q_create_ssr --> q_set_schema_ssr: set db.schema = "member"
    q_set_schema_ssr --> q_attach_cookies: configure cookie get/set/remove handlers
    q_attach_cookies --> [*]: return SSR client (RLS applies, user JWT from cookies)
    q_create_admin --> q_set_schema_admin: set db.schema = "member"
    q_set_schema_admin --> q_use_service_key: use SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY directly via @supabase/supabase-js
    q_use_service_key --> [*]: return admin client (RLS bypassed, no cookie/JWT dependency)

    note right of q_create_ssr
        INV-001: SSR client reads user JWT from cookies, causing RLS to evaluate as authenticated role
        INV-002: SSR client can only access rows permitted by RLS policies for the current user
    end note

    note right of q_create_admin
        INV-003: admin client MUST NOT use @supabase/ssr (SSR client reads JWT from cookies, silently returning 0 rows for UPDATE/DELETE)
        INV-004: admin client uses service role key to bypass RLS entirely
        INV-005: admin client must only be used in server-side contexts (never exposed to browser)
    end note

    note right of q_set_schema_ssr
        INV-006: all DB queries use the "member" schema (never change this schema name)
    end note
